    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the possible degrees of the remainder when a polynomial is divided by \\(2x^2 - 7x + 18\\), we need to consider the degree of the divisor polynomial. The divisor \\(2x^2 - 7x + 18\\) is a quadratic polynomial, since its degree is 2.\n\nWhen a polynomial is divided by a divisor of degree \\(d\\), the possible degrees of the remainder are less than the degree of the divisor. In this case, the divisor is \\(2x^2 - 7x + 18\\), which has a degree of 2. Therefore, the possible degrees of the remainder are 0, 1, or 2, but since the remainder must be a polynomial, the degree of the remainder must be less than the degree of the divisor. Thus, the possible degrees of the remainder are 0, 1.\n\nSo, the possible degrees of the remainder are \\(\\boxed{0, 1}\\).",
