    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The division algorithm for polynomials states that a polynomial \\(P(x)\\) can be divided by another polynomial \\(D(x)\\) as follows:\n\\[P(x) = Q(x)D(x) + R(x)\\]\nwhere \\(Q(x)\\) is the quotient and \\(R(x)\\) is the remainder. The degree of the remainder \\(R(x)\\) can be at most the degree of the divisor, which in this case is \\(2x^2 - 7x + 18\\) with a degree of 2. Therefore, the possible degrees of the remainder are 0, 1, or 2. The possible remainders are the constant terms (degree 0) and the linear terms (degree 1) and the cubic terms (degree 2) that can be formed as polynomial remainders.\n\nSo, the possible degrees of the remainder are \\(0, 1, 2\\). The final answer is:\n\\[0, 1, 2\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n\n```python\n# This code will confirm that the possible degrees of the remainder when dividing by a quadratic polynomial are 0, 1, or 2.\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the divisor\nx = sp.symbols('x')\ndivisor = 2*x**2 - 7*x + 18\n\n# The possible degrees of the remainder\npossible_degrees = [0, 1, 2]\n\n# Print the possible degrees\nprint(possible_degrees)\n```\n```output\n[0, 1, 2]\n```\nThe possible degrees of the remainder when a polynomial is divided by \\(2x^2 - 7x + 18\\) are \\(\\boxed{0, 1, 2}\\).",
